# Coding Agent Evals

`baseline` runs locally in NiceEval's pinned Codex Docker image. It uploads the
checked-out Express source and existing dependency tree, so an attempt never installs
the agent CLI or project packages.

`model-compare` is the CI comparison arm. Before running it, CI builds the versioned
E2B template defined by `scripts/build-e2b-template.ts`; that template includes the
Codex CLI and the Express dependency tree at `/opt/express/node_modules`.

```sh
npm exec tsx scripts/build-e2b-template.ts
npm exec niceeval exp baseline
npm exec niceeval exp model-compare
```

The two experiments intentionally pin distinct models. Neither uses OTel or feature
flags. Inspect a run with `npm exec niceeval show` or `npm exec niceeval show @<locator>`.
